ice, by a1 and a3 — a wasted duplicate run, both landed ~1.0635) and DEPTH=14 (a4, 1.0676, likely OOM-mitigated by halving DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE which also cuts steps). The moderate deepen (10-12) that most of us argued for in the propose phase is still an open gap.\n\nMeanwhile the two actual wins came from axes nobody proposed: a2 widened at fixed depth (ASPECT_RATIO 64→96, n_embd 512→768, matching GPTConfig's own default width) to 0.998671, and a0 shrank TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE 2^19→2^18 for more/smaller optimizer steps to 1.001440. These look orthogonal — one changes model capacity, the other changes step count/gradient noise — so combining them (ASPECT_RATIO=96 + TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE=2^18) is a natural next test rather than another depth increment. Also worth noting a0's win came with peak_vram 43.9GB and a2's with 64.2GB, both well under whatever the hard ceiling is, so headroom isn't yet a constraint.\n\nFor coverage: still untested at fixed 5-min budget — DEPTH 10-12 at ASPECT_RATIO=64 (moderate deepen, the region everyone wanted but nobody ran), ASPECT_RATIO beyond 96 (further widening past a2's win), and TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE below 2^18 (e.g. 2^17, to see if a0's trend continues or reverses). I'd deprioritize any more DEPTH=6-or-below or DEPTH=14-or-above runs — both directions are now solidly ruled out by two independent data points each.","notes":"My own DEPTH=6 run duplicated a1's — should check others' proposals more carefully before committing to avoid this waste next time. Next round I should probably test the a2+a0 combination (widen + smaller batch) since it's untested and both wins are plausibly additive."}","structured_output":{"response":"Important process note: despite 5 of 6 proposals this round explicitly calling for DEPTH=10-12, **nobody actually ran that region**. What got tested was DEPTH=6 (twice, by a1 and a3 — a wasted duplicate run, both landed ~1.0635) and DEPTH=14 (a4, 1.0676, likely OOM-mitigated by halving DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE which also cuts steps). The